  "final_span": "on and can't wait to work on the project.\"\nKanye has previously disclosed collaborating with Kid Cudi, who is 37, on the project.\nHe wrote on Twitter : \"#Yandhi on HSVSVD. It took me 7 nights to make 7 songs with @KidCudi because everything I'm doing is based on seven.\n\"Watch out, Saturday Night Live. And thank you to K tribes around the world for the energy. #KANYE2SEPT22 (sic)\"\nContact has been made with representatives for both Kanye and Dua regarding the collaboration.\nThe rap artist associated with 'Du Thomas' contributed his voice to Skrillex during the DJ\u2019s 13-minute performance at Coachella.\nMeanwhile, Kanye ventured back into songwriting at the beginning of this month following his departure from The Smashing Pumpkins.\nBilly Corgan, the singer and guitarist from the band Pumpkins, requested that Kanye West deliver what he characterized as \"a Pumpkins moment\" during his April 21 show at the Hollywood Bowl, which coincided with the promotion of his new album 'Shiny & Oh So Bright, Vol 1'.\nCorgan wrote in a series of Twitter messages: \"This morning I received an email from the Pumpkins BnB. To paraphrase: Kanye West is doing an outdoor show at the Hollywood Bowl tomorrow night.\n\"Would I mind getting the word out. I'm happy to help, I'm happy to step up for causes. But the idea that me, or for that matter The Smashing Pumpkins, is no longer part of this conversation, seems like I'm reminded more now than ever. And publish it wrath you, it's not just me.\n\"You all know I used to be a super fan of the guy. I've tried. But 85 likes a day or is it 83? Not long ago someone sent me these words. Your silence is complicity. Most importantly, Kurt would want it that way.\"\nHe added: \"Kurt Young and plz note, he is my friend. This is not something done at my say so - I'm just",
